  <string name="battery_fcm_explained">Notifications come as high-priority messages through the phone\'s push service, which wakes the app even in deep sleep. No battery setting needs to change.</string>
  <string name="battery_unifiedpush_explained">With UnifiedPush, the distributor app keeps the connection to the push server and wakes this app for each notification. The distributor must be allowed to run in the background: in its app settings, set battery use to unrestricted.</string>
  <string name="battery_vendor_hint">Some phones stop background apps on their own (for example after a while or when the screen is off). If notifications arrive late, look in the phone\'s battery or app-launch settings for this app and the distributor, and allow them to run in the background.</string>

